test_command=bash tests/harness_test.sh
id=harness-01 result=green reason=unit test "harness-01: a suite sourcing the harness library reproduces the copy-pasted helpers byte-for-byte (PASS/FAIL/SKIP shapes, accounting, exit status)" + "harness-01: registered-only-pass suite prints the frozen contract transcript and exits 0 exactly when no registered test failed" + "harness-01: a suite that sources tests/harness.sh defines none of the helpers itself and resolves them all from the library"
id=harness-02 result=green reason=unit tests "harness-02: new_tmp_dir creates under TMPDIR (or the /tmp fallback) and never under the repo working tree or the user config, leaving canary HOME/XDG empty" + "harness-02: every library render runs with HOME at a sandbox under temp space and XDG_CONFIG_HOME cleared, so install.sh writes only inside the sandbox" + "harness-02: no helper writes into the real ~/.claude, ~/.config/opencode, or ~/.config/antz while staging and rendering"
id=harness-03 result=green reason=unit tests "harness-03: rendering one staged tree twice executes install.sh exactly once and reuses the identical installed tree (contents and mtimes unchanged, still complete)" + "harness-03: rendering a different staged tree performs its own render, exercising that tree's staged state"
id=harness-04 result=skip reason=explicit skip stub in tests/harness_test.sh: the whole-area scan (only tests/harness.sh invokes install.sh) is the post-migration end state of all 38 suites, assigned by this change's README dependency note and this session's delegation to the later suite-migration sub-specs (02-09, re-asserted by hygiene 09); the library side it needs -- the single invocation point (install_at/install_xdg/render_tree) -- exists and is proven green by the harness-02/harness-03 tests
id=harness-05 result=skip reason=explicit skip stub in tests/harness_test.sh: the whole-area scan (every helper definition lives only in tests/harness.sh; suites keep registering their prior scenario ids) likewise completes only as the 38 suites migrate in sub-specs 02-09; the single-definition side is proven green today by "harness-01: a suite that sources tests/harness.sh defines none of the helpers itself and resolves them all from the library"
id=harness-06 result=green reason=unit tests "harness-06: cleanup removes every directory new_tmp_dir created for the run, also on early failure, leaving the TMPDIR root empty" + "harness-06: stage_checkout copies the working tree's current product files (install.sh, VERSION, CHANGELOG.md, agents/, scripts/orchestration/) into a fresh temp tree, with the optional VERSION override honored"
